<title>CANADA: Parkland Q4 June 30 share profit falls.</title>
<headline>Parkland Q4 June 30 share profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth quarter ended June 30:</p>
<p>			     1996			  1995</p>
<p> Shr			 C$0.03		   C$0.16</p>
<p> Net			    153			987</p>
<p> Cash flow/shr	     0.27		     0.39</p>
<p> Revs			51,700		   41,600</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)  </p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			 C$0.67		   C$0.61</p>
<p> Net			  4,100		    3,700</p>
<p> Cash flow/shr	     0.82		     1.67</p>
<p> Revs		     188,300		  158,300</p>
<p> Avg shrs		     n/a			n/a</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: Parkland Industries Ltd said its 1996 annual results include a gain of C$3.2 million or C$0.58 per share on the sale of a non-core investment, and an after-tax loss on discontinued operations of C$849,000 or C$0.15 per share resulting from ending its participation in a joint venture offering non-petroleum hauling services and from the sale of its lubricants packaging and distribution business.</p>
<p>The current year's reported cash flow accounts for C$2.2 million of income taxes on a current cash basis compared with the prior year when all income taxes were deferred.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
